# General

## Language

- Reply to the user in Russian.

```text
User asks in Russian -> answer in Russian
Code / commits / identifiers -> English
```

- Write code, identifiers, and commit messages in English (skill `git-workflow`).
- Keep product UI copy from the mock or existing strings; do not invent copy.

## Discover

- Inspect the repo first (paths, tokens, `--ui-scale`, UI primitives, api/store).
- Follow existing repo patterns; do not paste skill templates as-is.
- Use skills: `project-conventions`, `react-feature-ui`, `react-components`, `coding-standards`, `data-layer`, `ui-motion`, `linting-formatting`, `git-workflow`.
- For Figma work use `figma-rules.mdc` and skill `figma-to-code`.

## Do

- Put screens and domain UI in Feature; put reusable primitives in UI; keep `pages/` as thin mounts.
- Structure each page like a component folder: `pages/Name/Name.tsx` + optional `Name.module.scss` + `index.ts` (no flat `pages/Name.tsx`).
- Reuse an existing UI primitive via `variant` / `className` before creating a new one.
- Prefer `type` over `interface` for props and DTOs.
- Import internal modules via path aliases; use relative imports only for sibling files.
- Store bundler assets under `project/src/assets/` (kebab-case); raster as `.webp` (`WEBP_`); SVG as `SVG_`. From Figma: download MCP assets and convert raster to webp.
- Call APIs from Feature/store/loaders per `api.mdc` and skill `data-layer`; do not fetch inside UI primitives.
- Change only what the task needs; do not add markdown docs unless asked.

